---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Source Rights and Reuse | HUMANITY"
  description="How HUMANITY acquires, stores, attributes, and reviews third-party source material."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <header class="border-b border-humanity-border pb-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Transparency and reuse</p>
      <h1 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">
        Source rights &amp; reuse
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
        A source being listed or publicly accessible is not a license. Most
        publisher, feed, and report rights remain unreviewed. Narrow reuse
        permissions are documented for GDELT datasets and UCDP GED only.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section
      class="grid gap-5 border-b border-humanity-border py-8 sm:grid-cols-3"
      aria-label="Current source rights status"
    >
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Review status</p><p
          class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold"
        >
          Mixed; see register
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Commercial reuse</p><p
          class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold"
        >
          Dataset-only permissions
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">Redistribution</p><p
          class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold"
        >
          Dataset-only permissions
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <div
      class="prose-copy max-w-3xl space-y-7 py-8 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted"
    >
      <section>
        <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold text-humanity-text">
          What the pipeline handles
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Configured connectors can retrieve feed or API metadata and may fetch
          article-page text for candidate extraction. Fetched source records are
          persisted for processing. Public event pages link to originating
          reporting and may show short, attributed claim excerpts; full article
          republication is not intended.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          These technical behaviors are not a rights determination. Content
          access, storage duration, quotation, attribution requirements, and
          display permissions can differ by source and are still being reviewed.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GDELT's published terms allow commercial use and redistribution of its
          datasets with attribution; that does not cover linked publisher
          articles or media. UCDP GED datasets are CC BY 4.0 with attribution,
          but programmatic API access requires an approved token and no HUMANITY
          adapter is configured. News publishers, feeds, and ReliefWeb remain
          not cleared for commercial reuse or redistribution.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold text-humanity-text">
          Per-source register
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The machine-readable register records every configured connector and
          its review state. A test ensures new or removed source configurations
          cannot silently drift from that register.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            class="btn-secondary"
            href="https://github.com/asdfhgds/humanity/blob/master/config/source_rights.yaml"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Review source-rights register ↗</a
          >
          <a class="btn-secondary" href="/sources">Browse configured sources</a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold text-humanity-text">
          Before commercial use
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The project must verify terms and licenses, API/feed conditions,
          robots and rate limits, permitted content storage and retention,
          quotation and display scope, attribution, commercial use,
          redistribution, and privacy obligations for every connector. Qualified
          legal review is required. This page is a project disclosure, not legal
          advice or a grant of rights.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The software repository's MIT license applies to the software, not to
          third-party reporting, data, photographs, or other source material.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <p
      class="border-t border-humanity-border pt-5 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted"
    >
      For the complete operational notes, see <a
        class="link"
        href="https://github.com/asdfhgds/humanity/blob/master/docs/SOURCE_RIGHTS.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">the source-rights documentation</a
      >.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
